<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zog I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1895–1961</span> · Also known as Ahmet Zogu, King Zog, Zog I of Albania</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zog I, born Ahmet Zogu, was an Albanian chieftain from Mat who dominated his country's politics between the wars. He overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fan-noli">Fan Noli</a>'s government in December 1924, became president of the Albanian Republic in 1925 and proclaimed himself King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albanians">Albanians</a> in 1928. He drew Albania closely towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascist-italy">Fascist Italy</a>, which invaded in April 1939 and drove him into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zog-i.jpg" alt="Zog I" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was J.J. at English Wikipedia. (see en:Wikipedia:Upload log archive/April 2003); Tonysmith at z... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Zog_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
